            "text": "{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The conversation history before this point was compacted into the following summary:\\n\\n<summary>\\n## Goal\\nThe user is testing weather lookups with the `get_weather` tool: first a single-city query for Tokyo, then a parallel query for Tokyo and Paris with a one-sentence comparison.\\n\\n## Constraints & Preferences\\n- Use `get_weather` for lookups.\\n- Answers must be one short sentence.\\n- Parallel calls must be made in one step (the second request).\\n\\n## Progress\\n### Done\\n- [x] Called `get_weather(city=\\\"Tokyo\\\")` and answered: \\\"Tokyo is clear and 25°C, with 10 km/h wind.\\\"\\n- [x] Called `get_weather` for Tokyo and Paris in parallel in one step.\\n- [x] Reported Tokyo's weather and said no comparison was possible because Paris failed.\\n\\n### In Progress\\n- [ ] (none)\\n\\n### Blocked\\n- Paris weather unavailable: the tool returned \\\"Weather service unavailable for Paris\\\".\\n\\n## Key Decisions\\n- **Did not compare the cities**: Paris data was unavailable, so the assistant gave Tokyo's weather and explained the failure instead of guessing.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n1. If the user asks again, retry `get_weather(city=\\\"Paris\\\")` and compare it with Tokyo.\\n2. Otherwise wait for the user's next instruction.\\n\\n## Critical Context\\n- Tokyo result: \\\"Tokyo: clear25°C, wind 10 km/h\\\" (identical in both calls).\\n- Paris result: \\\"Weather service unavailable for Paris\\\" (may be transient).\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\\n\\n## Original Request\\nThe user asked what time it is in Tokyo. They told the assistant to use the get_time tool and then answer briefly.\\n\\n## Progress So Far\\n- The assistant called get_time(city=\\\"Tokyo\\\").\\n- The tool returned \\\"Tokyo: 09:00\\\".\\n- No final answer to the user is shown in these messages.\\n\\n## Context Needed to Continue\\n- The current time in Tokyo, per the tool result, is 09:00.\\n- The user wants a brief answer.\\n- The tool result gave no date, timezone label, or AM/PM designation beyond \\\"09:00\\\".\\n</summary>\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\":\"medium\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It's 09:00 in Tokyo.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Is that warm? One word.\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\":\"medium\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Yes.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Should I bring an umbrella? One word.\",\"cache_control\":{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"}}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\":\"medium\"}}],\"max_tokens\":128000,\"stream\":true,\"system\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"You are a weather assistant. Answer briefly.\\n\\n<addendum>\\nReference for pi-restore-anthropic-sonnet-5-5-combined: the weather desk's station catalog. Use it only when asked.\\n- Station 1: code WX001, elevation 0 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 2: code WX002, elevation 37 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 3: code WX003, elevation 74 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 4: code WX004, elevation 111 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 5: code WX005, elevation 148 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 6: code WX006, elevation 185 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 7: code WX007, elevation 222 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 8: code WX008, elevation 259 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 9: code WX009, elevation 296 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 10: code WX010, elevation 333 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 11: code WX011, elevation 370 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 12: code WX012, elevation 407 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 13: code WX013, elevation 444 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 14: code WX014, elevation 481 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 15: code WX015, elevation 518 m, reports hourl